# Which repository documents this skill carries, and how.
#
# Hand-authored on purpose: adding a doc to the repo must never silently
# enlarge the skill. A line here is a deliberate decision that an agent
# building with verdict needs this document.
#
# Format:  tier <TAB> source-path-in-repo <TAB> destination-under-references/
#
#   bundled  copied into the artifact by scripts/build.sh. Available with no
#            network and no round trip. Keep this set small — it is read on
#            every invocation that needs it.
#   fetch    NOT shipped. Pulled on demand from the repository at the tag
#            matching the consumer's installed version. See SKILL.md.
#
# A trailing slash on both sides copies a directory.
#
# Deliberately absent, and not by oversight:
#   docs/maintenance.md, docs/adding-a-language.md, docs/future_plan.md
#     — maintainer documents. A consumer changing their own rules never needs
#       them, and shipping them would spend an agent's context on this repo's
#       internals rather than on the caller's problem.
#   fixtures/graduation_verdict/
#     — the cross-language parity fixture. It exists to prove a new language
#       port matches the reference, which is a contributor activity.
#       docs/adding-a-language.md routes contributors there; SKILL.md mentions
#       it for an agent that wants a worked example of testing rule-based
#       logic, without spending routing surface on it.
#   python/examples/graduation_verdict/*.py and its data files
#     — example *code*. An agent reads the pattern from the example's own
#       docs; shipping the project itself would put a pyproject.toml, and in
#       other languages a .csproj or pubspec.yaml, inside a consumer's skill
#       directory.

bundled	docs/architecture.md	docs/architecture.md
bundled	docs/extension.md	docs/extension.md

fetch	docs/testing.md	docs/testing.md
fetch	python/docs/quickstart.md	python/quickstart.md
fetch	python/docs/samples/	python/samples/
fetch	python/examples/graduation_verdict/README.md	python/example/README.md
fetch	python/examples/graduation_verdict/docs/architecture.md	python/example/architecture.md
fetch	python/examples/graduation_verdict/docs/testing.md	python/example/testing.md
